# Per-Dockerfile ignore file — governs builds run with `-f Dockerfile` (the hub
# image). BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` and then does NOT read the
# shared `.dockerignore`, so this file is the *entire* ignore set for that build
# and both lists must be kept in step (see REFERENCE.md §Build-context layout).
# It has to cover a parent-context build as well as this repo's root:
#   - this repo's root — CI and release builds, where the patterns below are
#     exactly `.dockerignore`'s, so those builds are unchanged by this file existing;
#   - a parent workspace directory, where this repo is a subdirectory. The final
#     block holds the nested forms that only matter there, and matches nothing in a
#     CI checkout. Nothing uses that context today (the demo build that did now
#     lives in the private mushpi-demo-infra repo); the block is kept inert.
# Everything below is excluded from the context upload; nothing a `COPY` in the
# Dockerfile reads may match — `mushpi-server/` and `mushpi-client/` are build
# inputs and must NEVER be listed.

# VCS
.git
**/.git

# Dependencies + build output — rebuilt inside the image
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
.yarn/cache
**/.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz

# Runtime data — must never be baked into the image
data
mushpi-data
data-test
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Secrets
.env
.env.prod
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.prod
**/.env.local

# Build tooling not needed in the context
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
README.md

# Sub-repos that are never build inputs (keep the context lean).
# NOTE: mushpi-server and mushpi-client are the build inputs — the Dockerfile
# COPYs from both — and must NEVER be listed in this file.
# mushpi-grow / mushpi-mock DO land in this root — checked out on v* tag builds
# (the verify-release.sh parity check) and by the local verify recipe — but they
# are never COPY sources, so they stay listed. mushpi-docs is absent on purpose:
# nothing materializes it here.
mushpi-grow
mushpi-mock

# IDE / hooks
.vscode
.idea
.husky

# --- Parent-context additions -------------------------------------------------
# Only reachable when the context is the workspace directory holding this repo:
# the same state, secrets and non-input repos one level down, plus the sibling
# clones that sit *inside* it. Inert in a CI checkout of this repo alone. Nothing
# here may match a `COPY` source — `**/data` is deliberately absent for that
# reason (the server's and client's source trees are what a `data/` directory
# would otherwise swallow).
**/.venv
**/mushpi-data
**/data-test
**/mushpi-grow
**/mushpi-mock
.opencode
docs
